# Build artifacts
dist/
bin/
*.test
*.out
coverage.txt

# Default `go build ./...` from repo root emits a binary named after the
# module's last path segment ("pyrycode-relay") into CWD. Anchored with
# leading slash so it matches the repo-root binary only, not any future
# package directory of the same name. Same shape as the .codegraph fix
# below — auto-commit safety nets need a trustworthy gitignore. Salvage
# on PR #27 swept the binary in before this entry existed.
/pyrycode-relay

# Go
go.work
go.work.sum

# Editor
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# Logs / runtime
*.log
.cert-cache/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# CodeGraph index (used by dispatcher worktree symlink + interactive
# Claude Code sessions for symbol-level code intel — local cache only).
# No trailing slash: matches both directories AND symlinks. The trailing
# slash variant `.codegraph/` only matches directories, which let the
# dispatcher's worktree symlink at `<wt>/.codegraph` slip past gitignore
# and get auto-committed in pyrycode (commit 30f3d53). Same fix here
# defensively before the same chain bites this repo.
.codegraph
